---
description: Canonical operating guide for this Elementor page-building repo
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root — it is the canonical, tool-agnostic operating
guide (process, folder convention, standards, tooling). `CLAUDE.md` and `GEMINI.md`
are equivalent stubs pointing to the same file.

Route the task first. **Most tasks are the third row.**

- Doc/brief for an **already-onboarded** site (`projects/<site>/skills/` exists) →
  skip straight to building the page. This is the common case.
- Site with an **exported Elementor kit**, not yet onboarded → `scripts/analyze-kit.py`
  then `skills/elementor-kit-onboarding`.
- Site with **no kit** (HTML/CSS prototype, or brand new) → `design-source/`, then
  `scripts/analyze-prototype.py` and `skills/html-prototype-onboarding`.

Both onboarding paths converge on `projects/<site>/tokens.json`. Everything after
that is identical and origin-agnostic.

Build a page: source doc into `projects/<site>/pages/<page-slug>/`, author
`build.py` on the site's `brand.py` (or `scripts/elementor_builder.py`), then
`python3 scripts/validate-page.py <page>.json` must exit 0, then
`python3 scripts/make-preview.py <page>.json`. Deliverable is the page JSON plus
`HANDOFF-notes.md`.

Match the kit; don't redesign it. Build through the generated `<site>-*` skills,
never from an ad-hoc read of the kit. Emit complete JSON — no elisions. The client's
install usually is not reachable: verify with the preview or a local throwaway
WordPress (`scripts/sandbox.sh`), never against their live site.
